+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. Export
+`createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`, returning a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into `to`
+when applied, without mutating either input, and describing what changed and nothing more (no resending
+of the whole document for a small change).
+
+## What was done
+
+- Design recorded in dl-005-createpatch-minimal-structural-diff-lcs-for-arrays-json-values-only-jsonpatcherror.
+- `test/create-patch.test.ts`: 17 tests written first (red: the export did not exist): equal documents,
+  member order, nested replace, added/removed members, `null` members, type changes, token escaping,
+  array insertions/removals/in-place changes, mixed array edits, a small change in a 2000-element list
+  giving one operation, large arrays past the alignment bound, no mutation and no sharing, `__proto__`,
+  null-prototype objects and shared sub-values, non-JSON inputs.
+- `src/index.ts`: `createPatch`, with an LCS-based array diff, reusing `isJsonValue`, `cloneJson`,
+  `jsonEqual` and `isObject`.
+- `README.md`: a "Creating a JSON Patch" section.
+- `npm test`: 82 tests pass. A throwaway seeded fuzz check (20,000 random pairs, not committed) confirmed
+  `applyPatch(a, createPatch(a, b))` equals `b`. `tsc` is not installed here, so the type check was not run.
